<title>USA: Rutherford-Moran sets '97 capital spending.</title>
<headline>Rutherford-Moran sets '97 capital spending.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rutherford-Moran Oil Corp said on Tuesday that it expects capital spending to be $108 million in 1997, including $28 million in funds to buy Maersk Oil (Thailand) Ltd.</p>
<p>The company, which concentrates its activities in Southeast Asia, said other funds will be spent on platform development and drilling in the Tantawan Field, fabrication efforts for facilities and exploration in Benchamas and other 3-D seismic acquisitions.</p>
<p>The Maersk acquisition will add reserves of 50 billion cubic feet of gas to reserves, Rutherford-Moran said.</p>
<p>Rutherford-Moran conducted an initial public stock offering in June 1996.</p>
</text>
